      "post_id": "122143029440775283",
      "author_id": "61573258492545",
      "author_name": "Alan Juarez",
      "message": "🎭 Kabuki: Japan’s Living Masterpiece of Drama 🇯🇵 This stunning costume isn’t just clothing—it’s centuries of Japanese tradition brought to life. Kabuki is one of Japan’s most iconic performing arts, dating back over 400 years. Every detail has meaning: 🎭 The bold white makeup highlights the actor’s expressions. 🎨 The dramatic red lines symbolize courage, strength, and justice. 👘 The elaborate costume and towering wig can weigh over 20 kilograms, requiring years of training to perform gracefully. Originally, Kabuki was performed by women in the early 1600s. Today, all traditional Kabuki roles—including female characters—are performed by highly skilled male actors known as Onnagata, who spend decades mastering elegant movements and expressions. Recognized by UNESCO as an Intangible Cultural Heritage, Kabuki continues to captivate audiences with its powerful storytelling, music, dance, and breathtaking stage effects. Watching Kabuki isn’t just seeing a performance—it’s stepping into Japan",
